WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.840
Darth Vader reigns supreme as&nbsp;
the greatest bad guy the Star&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.720
Wars franchise has ever seen. That&nbsp;
being said, here are some franchise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:12.800
villains who are arguably even scarier&nbsp;
and more powerful than Vader himself.

00:00:12.800 --> 00:00:17.720
When discussing iconic villains outside of the&nbsp;
core Star Wars movies, one has to mention Grand&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:23.240
Admiral Thrawn. The stoic Chiss strategist&nbsp;
helped resurrect Star Wars in the 1990s, with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.240 --> 00:00:28.240
Timothy Zahn's beloved Heir to the Empire novels&nbsp;
jump-starting interest in the franchise again.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:38.341
"Where is your master? Where&nbsp;
is Grand Admiral Thrawn?"

00:00:38.341 --> 00:00:42.200
Though he was briefly expunged from the&nbsp;
canon after Disney took over the franchise,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:47.760
Thrawn returned in Star Wars Rebels and has become&nbsp;
increasingly important to the modern timeline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:47.760 --> 00:00:52.560
He's the primary villain of the live-action&nbsp;
Ahsoka on Disney+, and for good reason.

00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:57.320
Thrawn is a truly terrifying individual.&nbsp;
Sure, he may not have the hulking black suit,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.320 --> 00:01:03.240
murderous Force powers, or imposing red lightsaber&nbsp;
Darth Vader has, but in a way, that only makes him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:03.240 --> 00:01:09.400
more intimidating. Aside from his bright red eyes&nbsp;
and cold blue skin, he looks pretty normal. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:14.440
that unassuming exterior hides one of the most&nbsp;
brilliant and brutal minds in all of Star Wars.

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:18.760
Though he occasionally hesitates before taking&nbsp;
innocent lives, Thrawn is usually willing to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:23.560
do anything necessary to win. And his Legends&nbsp;
incarnation is even more frightening than the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:28.600
new canon Thrawn, though Disney still has a&nbsp;
lot of places it could take the character.

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:32.720
Stepping back into the modern Star Wars canon,&nbsp;
we've got the shadowy leader of the Nightsisters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:38.240
of Dathomir, Mother Talzin. Talzin primarily&nbsp;
appears as a secondary antagonist in Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.240 --> 00:01:41.760
The Clone Wars, where she aids&nbsp;
her "children" Asajj Ventress,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:46.400
Savage Opress, and Maul in their battles&nbsp;
against Darth Sidious and Count Dooku.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:46.400 --> 00:01:51.480
She puts a lot of innocent people in danger&nbsp;
through her dark Force schemes of conquest.

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:55.440
"I must make the necessary preparations."

00:01:55.440 --> 00:01:59.880
Talzin may not be as overtly intimidating&nbsp;
or good in a fight as Darth Vader or many&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.880 --> 00:02:04.600
other characters on this list. However, she&nbsp;
makes the cut for slightly different reasons.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:07.840
Even though she hasn’t attempted&nbsp;
to take over the Galactic Senate,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:11.080
her Force powers are beyond&nbsp;
almost anyone else in the canon.

00:02:11.080 --> 00:02:15.280
Talzin's magical abilities are never fully&nbsp;
explained, which is also what makes them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:19.720
so dangerous. Throughout The Clone Wars, she&nbsp;
demonstrates a mastery of the dark arts that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:24.600
allows for full mind control, the ability&nbsp;
to cheat death through spiritual means,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:24.600 --> 00:02:28.520
and the power to turn other life forms&nbsp;
into incredibly powerful and violent&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:33.200
soldiers. Darth Sidious considers her a&nbsp;
direct rival, and he goes out of his way&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.240
to deal with her in The Clone Wars after&nbsp;
her interference in his plans. If you've&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:42.480
got Sheev knocking on your front door, you know&nbsp;
you're doing something right – or, well, wrong.

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:47.440
Though villains like Revan and Nihilus may be more&nbsp;
famous than The Old Republic foe Darth Malgus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.440 --> 00:02:51.760
their stories are also more complicated,&nbsp;
which is part of their appeal. Malgus,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.760 --> 00:02:55.840
on the other hand, is a villain&nbsp;
in every sense of the word.

00:02:55.840 --> 00:02:59.520
"Finally, we have returned."

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:04.440
A brutal tactician and fearsome warrior, Malgus&nbsp;
wrote the playbook Darth Vader uses when he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:08.920
sacks the Jedi Temple at the end of the Clone&nbsp;
Wars. Malgus took over the stronghold several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.920 --> 00:03:14.520
thousand years earlier, wiping out numerous Jedi&nbsp;
masters and effectively shattering the order.

00:03:14.520 --> 00:03:17.320
Malgus was a force in the galaxy for years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:21.680
putting Jedi and fellow Sith alike in&nbsp;
their place and establishing himself as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:21.680 --> 00:03:26.240
a dark Force boogeyman. Plus, just&nbsp;
look at the guy. He's terrifying!

00:03:26.240 --> 00:03:29.880
Some of the characters on this list&nbsp;
are beings of pure dark Force energy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:34.760
leaders of powerful military legions,&nbsp;
and ruthless murderers. Dagan Gera is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.760 --> 00:03:40.240
none of those things. He's a former Jedi whose&nbsp;
obsession and ego lead him down a dark path,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:44.360
eventually forgoing everything and&nbsp;
everyone he once claimed to fight for.

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:48.920
"How arrogant that you would&nbsp;
presume to know what drives me!"

00:03:48.920 --> 00:03:52.240
When you first meet Dagan Gera&nbsp;
in Star Wars Jedi: Survivor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.240 --> 00:03:56.320
it's not unusual to just feel bad for&nbsp;
the guy. During the High Republic era,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.320 --> 00:04:00.240
hundreds of years before the original Star&nbsp;
Wars trilogy, Dagan was one of the order's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:04.760
most powerful and respected knights. In the&nbsp;
time since he was put into stasis, the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.760 --> 00:04:10.360
Jedi Order was destroyed. However, these initial&nbsp;
feelings of sympathy are quickly replaced by fear.

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:14.640
Dagan may not have the warlord persona of Darth&nbsp;
Vader, but it's hard to watch him in motion and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:19.280
not feel unnerved. He looks, walks, and&nbsp;
talks like a ghost — a clear reflection&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:24.760
of his status as a man out of time. His icy&nbsp;
eyes and cold, determined energy are imposing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.760 --> 00:04:29.240
to say the least, and that's without even&nbsp;
getting into Dagan's power as a fighter.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:29.240 --> 00:04:33.680
He pushes Cal Kestis to his limit with&nbsp;
only one arm, and his skill at projecting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.800
illusions through the Force is beyond&nbsp;
anything previously seen in the canon.

00:04:37.800 --> 00:04:41.960
The dark side is more than just a cool&nbsp;
goth aesthetic, but nobody told The Son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:41.960 --> 00:04:46.560
that. He's also crazy powerful: as one&nbsp;
of the three Force Wielders of Mortis,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:51.000
also known simply as "The Ones," The Son&nbsp;
is an ancient being of immense power whose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:51.000 --> 00:04:55.360
very essence is intrinsically connected to&nbsp;
the Force. And while his sister got to be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:55.360 --> 00:04:59.560
part of the light side, The Son — through no&nbsp;
choice of his own — was stuck with the dark.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:07.760
"How simple you make it. Light and dark,&nbsp;
as if there is one without the other."

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:11.640
The Mortis arc of Star Wars: The Clone&nbsp;
Wars shows just how terrifying The Son&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:16.000
can be. Not only is he an incredibly&nbsp;
powerful Force user in his own right,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:20.760
capable of high-level combat abilities and&nbsp;
full-on transformation into a massive beast,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.760 --> 00:05:25.440
but he can take over the minds of other people&nbsp;
and twist them toward the dark. His father&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.440 --> 00:05:29.800
suggests that The Son escaping from Mortis&nbsp;
could doom the entire galaxy. Fortunately,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:29.800 --> 00:05:35.080
Anakin, Obi-Wan, and Ahsoka Tano manage&nbsp;
to stop the Son before that happens.

00:05:35.080 --> 00:05:39.840
Star Wars Knights of the Old Republic II: The&nbsp;
Sith Lords introduced several great characters,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:42.680
including the dark Sith Lord Darth Traya.

00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:49.120
"There will always be a Darth Traya.&nbsp;
The galaxy needs its betrayers."

00:05:49.120 --> 00:05:54.480
What sets Traya apart from the other Sith on this&nbsp;
list, and even from her one-time allies Darth Sion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:59.760
and Darth Nihilus, is her utter disdain for the&nbsp;
Force itself. Traya views the Force as a god of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:05.120
sorts — one that forces its will on every being&nbsp;
in the galaxy, trapping them in its eternal plan.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.120 --> 00:06:09.720
For this reason, she wants to free the galaxy from&nbsp;
its influence — something that no other villain in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:09.720 --> 00:06:14.360
all of Star Wars has ever attempted. The sheer&nbsp;
scale of Traya's scheme puts her in a class by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:14.360 --> 00:06:20.200
herself — a harbinger of destruction who truly&nbsp;
believes that her way is the best for the galaxy.

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:24.720
We'd be remiss not to include a villain from the&nbsp;
Star Wars High Republic era on this list, and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.720 --> 00:06:29.480
obvious choice is Marchion Ro. The leader of the&nbsp;
deadly marauder band known as the Nihil, Marchion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:29.480 --> 00:06:34.880
Ro is directly responsible for causing the&nbsp;
so-called "Great Hyperspace Disaster," which kicks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.880 --> 00:06:39.600
off the High Republic arc and leads to widespread&nbsp;
destruction and death across the galaxy.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:44.960
Though he's ostensibly just a pirate, Ro devises a&nbsp;
plan that puts the Jedi on the back foot. His most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.960 --> 00:06:49.480
terrifying weapons are the Nameless, ruthless&nbsp;
monsters who hunt down anyone strong in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:49.480 --> 00:06:54.120
Force. Quite literally boogeymen for the Jedi,&nbsp;
the Nameless are used to great effect during&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.120 --> 00:06:58.800
Marchion Ro's conquests. He can't Force-choke&nbsp;
you or shoot lightning out of his hands,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:04.560
but he shows just how powerful someone can become&nbsp;
simply through strategy, determination, and fear.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:04.560 --> 00:07:10.480
Ro causes more chaos than most Sith Lords ever&nbsp;
have, earning him an easy spot on this list.

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.040
In both Legends and the modern Star&nbsp;
Wars canon, Darth Bane is the creator&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.040 --> 00:07:18.680
of the "Rule of Two" — the Sith doctrine that&nbsp;
dictates there can only be one master and one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:23.160
apprentice of the order at any given time.
 
Roughly 1,000 years before the prequels,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:27.800
the Sith were wiped out by a combination of&nbsp;
their war with the Jedi, constant infighting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.800 --> 00:07:32.640
and Bane's efforts to eradicate them from within.&nbsp;
Prior to Bane instituting the Rule of Two,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.640 --> 00:07:36.960
the Sith were a sprawling order much like the&nbsp;
Jedi. He believed that the only way for them&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:42.080
to be strong enough to survive was to consolidate&nbsp;
power in as few people as possible. The rule was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:42.080 --> 00:07:46.160
designed from the beginning with this goal in&nbsp;
mind: a master to wield the full brunt of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:46.160 --> 00:07:50.920
dark side and an apprentice to keep the master&nbsp;
on their toes. The inherent tension between the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:50.920 --> 00:07:55.000
two would ensure that the most powerful&nbsp;
person possible would always be on top.

00:07:55.000 --> 00:07:59.480
His importance to the history of Star Wars is&nbsp;
enough to land him on a list of notable villains,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:03.800
but Bane is intimidating enough in his own&nbsp;
right to earn a spot here. Plenty of Sith&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:08.800
have wiped out innocents and Jedi, but Bane&nbsp;
seemingly wiped out the rest of the Sith,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.560
proving himself a true villain among villains.

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:16.040
Born Jacen Solo, the son of Han and Leia,&nbsp;
Darth Caedus is one of the most famous and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:16.040 --> 00:08:20.800
powerful villains in the Legends timeline.&nbsp;
He fights valiantly in the Yuuzhan Vong War&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.800 --> 00:08:24.480
but never truly recovers from the loss&nbsp;
of his younger brother, Anakin Solo,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:29.360
or the torture he suffers during the war. Jacen's&nbsp;
fall to the dark side is one of the longest,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:34.600
most fully developed storylines in the entire&nbsp;
Expanded Universe, culminating in a tragic climax.

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:38.680
Darth Caedus is downright terrifying and&nbsp;
one of the most powerful Force users in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:42.800
all of Star Wars. Few characters are ever&nbsp;
able to match him in a lightsaber duel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:42.800 --> 00:08:48.080
and even his uncle Luke Skywalker, at the height&nbsp;
of his powers, struggles immensely to defeat him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:52.520
His Force powers are among the most outrageous&nbsp;
in the history of the franchise: Caedus learns&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:52.520 --> 00:08:57.600
to ignore all pain, and at one point, even&nbsp;
becomes one with the Force while still alive.

00:08:57.600 --> 00:09:01.640
Darth Krayt certainly isn't the most famous&nbsp;
villain from the Star Wars Legends timeline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:01.640 --> 00:09:05.520
But in a way, he's the most important&nbsp;
villain in the entire Expanded Universe.

00:09:05.520 --> 00:09:08.440
Krayt's journey starts the&nbsp;
way so many Sith stories do:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:08.440 --> 00:09:13.080
being trained as a Jedi. Under his birth name&nbsp;
of A'Sharad Hett, he was a young member of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:17.160
order during the prequel era and fought&nbsp;
alongside Anakin Skywalker in the Clone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:17.160 --> 00:09:21.760
Wars. But it's not until decades later that&nbsp;
he becomes a proper player in the story.

00:09:21.760 --> 00:09:26.560
A series of Sith encounters and brutal clashes&nbsp;
with the Yuuzhan Vong lead Krayt down a path&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.560 --> 00:09:31.520
to the dark side. He becomes the leader of a&nbsp;
secret Sith sect, briefly emerges to help Luke&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.520 --> 00:09:36.680
Skywalker defeat Abeloth, but then goes back&nbsp;
into hiding. Through various bouts of stasis&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:36.680 --> 00:09:41.720
and a literal death and resurrection arc, Krayt&nbsp;
lives far into the future, eventually crossing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:41.720 --> 00:09:46.360
lightsabers with Luke and Anakin's distant&nbsp;
descendant Cade Skywalker during the Star Wars:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:46.360 --> 00:09:51.440
Legacy series. Beyond all that, Krayt is a true&nbsp;
master of the Force and one of the main reasons&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:51.440 --> 00:09:57.840
that Jacen Solo turns to the dark side. Even Luke&nbsp;
Skywalker comes to fear the so-called "Dark Man."

00:09:57.840 --> 00:10:01.600
It's kind of cheating to put two different&nbsp;
characters in the same spot on this list,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.600 --> 00:10:04.880
but there's a good reason for it. To&nbsp;
be honest, the Yuuzhan Vong as a whole&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:08.120
species could have their own ranking&nbsp;
here. In the entirety of Star Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:08.120 --> 00:10:12.680
there may not be a more horrifying foe. But&nbsp;
in the interest of keeping things specific,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:18.360
we're focusing on two particular Yuuzhan Vong —&nbsp;
Shimrra Jamaane, the Supreme Overlord during the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:18.360 --> 00:10:22.880
Yuuzhan Vong War, and Onimi, who's pulling&nbsp;
the strings of the war from the shadows.

00:10:22.880 --> 00:10:27.720
In a way, these two characters are the same.&nbsp;
Shimrra is the face, and Onimi is the mind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:27.720 --> 00:10:31.800
The plan to invade the Star Wars galaxy and&nbsp;
assimilate it into the Vong's distorted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:36.720
biohacked hellscape comes from Onimi, and the&nbsp;
many warriors of these zealous conquerors put it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.720 --> 00:10:42.000
into practice. The Yuuzhan Vong War is the single&nbsp;
most devastating event in the Expanded Universe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:48.040
wiping out countless lives and numerous beloved&nbsp;
characters, including Chewbacca and Anakin Solo.

00:10:48.040 --> 00:10:52.680
The Vong are horrifying to look at, they use&nbsp;
torture as a standard method of breaking and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.680 --> 00:10:57.680
corrupting prisoners, and with only a couple of&nbsp;
exceptions, like Onimi, they have absolutely zero&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.680 --> 00:11:08.120
connection to the Force. And no two Vong are more&nbsp;
scary or powerful than Onimi and Shimrra Jamaane.

